Subject: [PATCH 02856/11362] [outer-loop] ARC Level-Up Attempt Guarantee:
 forcing function + lint (operator 2026-06-19)

Operator: "ensure we ALWAYS have at least one level-up attempt across all games once a roadmap." The
ARC sprint's headline metric is reproducible_total_levels growing, but a planner can drift to all-meta
(library induction, benchmarks, hygiene, packaging, generic re-solves of already-banked levels) and
ship a roadmap with ZERO level-bank attempts = churn. Added scripts/arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py
(counts tasks whose gate requires offline_reproduced=true AND a NEW-level condition -- first-contact an
unsolved game OR +1 deeper on a solved one; exit 1 if < --min, default 1; prints targeted games for
rotation audit) + a CLAUDE.md MANDATORY forcing function (every ARC-sprint roadmap >=1 level-up
attempt; rotate targets across games; lint is the backstop, activation-guard wiring pending). Validated:
.412 PASSES (4 attempts: dc22 solve, sc25 deepen, first-contact a new game, tr87 generic); an all-meta
roadmap FAILS exit 1.

